---- ENDF/B-VIII.1    MATERIAL 2600         REVISION 1            2600 1451
----- ELECTRO-ATOMIC INTERACTION DATA                             2600 1451
------ ENDF-6                                                     2600 1451
==================================================================2600 1451
The Livermore Evaluated Electron Data Library (EEDL) in the       2600 1451
ENDF-6 Format. Translated from the Livermore ENDL format          2600 1451
to the ENDF-6 Format.                                             2600 1451
==================================================================2600 1451
  Contents                                                        2600 1451
==================================================================2600 1451
  MF/MT    Description                                            2600 1451
==================================================================2600 1451
  23/501   Total Electron Cross Sections                          2600 1451
  23/522   Ionization (sum of subshells)                          2600 1451
  23/525   Large Angle Elastic Scattering Cross Section           2600 1451
  23/526   Elastic Scatter (Total) Cross Sections                 2600 1451
  23/527   Bremsstrahlung Cross Sections                          2600 1451
  23/528   Excitation Cross Sections                              2600 1451
  23/534   K (1S1/2)    Electroionization Subshell Cross Sections 2600 1451
  23/535   L1 (2s1/2)   Electroionization Subshell Cross Sections 2600 1451
  23/536   L2 (2p1/2)   Electroionization Subshell Cross Sections 2600 1451
  23/537   L3 (2p3/2)   Electroionization Subshell Cross Sections 2600 1451
  23/538   M1 (3s1/2)   Electroionization Subshell Cross Sections 2600 1451
  23/539   M2 (3p1/2)   Electroionization Subshell Cross Sections 2600 1451
  23/540   M3 (3p3/2)   Electroionization Subshell Cross Sections 2600 1451
  23/541   M4 (3d3/2)   Electroionization Subshell Cross Sections 2600 1451
  23/542   M5 (3d5/2)   Electroionization Subshell Cross Sections 2600 1451
  23/543   N1 (4s1/2)   Electroionization Subshell Cross Sections 2600 1451
==================================================================2600 1451
  26/525   Large Angle Elastic Angular Distributions              2600 1451
  26/527   Bremsstrahlung Photon Energy Spectra and               2600 1451
                          Electron Average Energy Loss            2600 1451
  26/528   Excitation Electron Average Energy Loss                2600 1451
  26/534   K (1S1/2)    Electroionization Subshell Energy Spectra 2600 1451
  26/535   L1 (2s1/2)   Electroionization Subshell Energy Spectra 2600 1451
  26/536   L2 (2p1/2)   Electroionization Subshell Energy Spectra 2600 1451
  26/537   L3 (2p3/2)   Electroionization Subshell Energy Spectra 2600 1451
  26/538   M1 (3s1/2)   Electroionization Subshell Energy Spectra 2600 1451
  26/539   M2 (3p1/2)   Electroionization Subshell Energy Spectra 2600 1451
  26/540   M3 (3p3/2)   Electroionization Subshell Energy Spectra 2600 1451
  26/541   M4 (3d3/2)   Electroionization Subshell Energy Spectra 2600 1451
  26/542   M5 (3d5/2)   Electroionization Subshell Energy Spectra 2600 1451
  26/543   N1 (4s1/2)   Electroionization Subshell Energy Spectra 2600 1451
==================================================================2600 1451
  Warning                                                         2600 1451
==================================================================2600 1451
  MF/MT combinations used to define ALL electron interaction data 2600 1451
  are newly defined MF/MT numbers for ENDF/B-VI that did not exist2600 1451
  in earlier versions of ENDF/B.                                  2600 1451
==================================================================2600 1451
  Definition of Data                                              2600 1451
==================================================================2600 1451
  Cross Sections (MF=23)                                          2600 1451
==================================================================2600 1451
1) The total electron interaction cross section is given          2600 1451
   explicitly as MF/MT=23/501. It is the sum of scatter,          2600 1451
   bremsstrahlung, excitation and ionization cross sections,      2600 1451
   i.e., MT = 526, 527, 528, and 534 through 572.                 2600 1451
2) The total electron ionization cross section is given           2600 1451
   explicitly as MF/MT=23/522. It is the sum of the aubshell      2600 1451
   cross sections, i.e., all MT = 534 through 572.                2600 1451
==================================================================2600 1451
  Angular and Energy Distributions (MF=26)                        2600 1451
==================================================================2600 1451
3) For Large Angle Scatter (MT=525), angular distributions of     2600 1451
   electrons are tabulated between cosine = -1.0 and 0.999999.    2600 1451
   Between +0.99999 and +1.0 it is analytically defined as        2600 1451
   Coulomb scattering,                                            2600 1451
                                                                  2600 1451
   d(sig)/d(cos) = A/[eta+(1.0 - cos)]^2                          2600 1451
                                                                  2600 1451
   where the shielding parameter (eta) is defined by the          2600 1451
   Steve Seltzer expression (see, ref. 1), and (A) is the         2600 1451
   normalization factor for the integral +0.99999 to +1.0.        2600 1451
   Electron elastic scatter means no energy loss, so only         2600 1451
   angular distributions are giving.                              2600 1451
4) For bremsstrahlung, both the outgoing electron and photon are  2600 1451
   described. The photon energy spectra are given, but angular    2600 1451
   distributions are not; these can be analytically defined by a  2600 1451
   number of different methods. For the electron, average energy  2600 1451
   loss is given. The electron is assumed to continue along its   2600 1451
   original direction of travel, so angular distributions are not 2600 1451
   given. WARNING - bremsstrahlung is a three body process,       2600 1451
   involving an electron, a photon, and an atom - so that you     2600 1451
   cannot use energy or momentum correlation to simply relate     2600 1451
   the secondary electron and the emitted photon.                 2600 1451
5) For excitation, the average energy loss of the electron is     2600 1451
   given. The electron is assumed to continue along its original  2600 1451
   direction of travel, so angular distributions are not given.   2600 1451
6) For Ionization, the spectra of electrons is given. The electron2600 1451
   is assumed to continue along its original direction of travel, 2600 1451
   so angular distributions are not given. In ionization two      2600 1451
   identical electrons emerge; the incident electron, and an      2600 1451
   electron ejected by the atom [thereby ionizing the atom]. Since2600 1451
   the two particles are indistinquishable, we define the electron2600 1451
   with the lower energy to be that ejected by the atom, and the  2600 1451
   electron with the higher energy to be the incident electron.   2600 1451
   The energy of the two electrons is exactly correlated by energy2600 1451
   conservation: initial incident electron energy = binding energy2600 1451
   of the ejected electron, plus the kinetic energy of the ejected2600 1451
   and the secondary incident electron. Therefore only the spectra2600 1451
   of the lower energy, ejected electron is given. The energy of  2600 1451
   the secondary incident electron should be defined to conserve  2600 1451
   energy, as described above. The energy lost by the incident    2600 1451
   electron is the sum of the binding and kinetic energy of the   2600 1451
   ejected electron.                                              2600 1451
7) Relaxation of ionized atoms back to neutrality is not described2600 1451
   here; it is described in the companion Evaluated Atomic Data   2600 1451
   Library (EADL).                                                2600 1451
